# A digit-string literal beyond even `long`, in Clipping's far-plane float
# slot. strtol saturates it at LONG_MAX, which itself exceeds RtInt's
# range, so GMANRIBTokenize::parseNum's range check rejects it with
# RIE_RANGE where it is tokenized, before nextFloat ever sees it --
# nextFloat carries no RtInt bound of its own. See
# clipping_float_slot_rtint_overflow.rib for the other former failure
# range (a literal that fits `long` but not RtInt) reaching this same
# float slot.
#
# A trailing Sphere follows AGENTS.md's "RIB authoring" section, "The
# desync convention."
Display "malformed_out.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 99999999999999999999
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
WorldEnd
